       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the indication, and amlodipine 50 mg once daily is well outside any labeled or guideline-supported dosing. The maximum is 10 mg daily. I don't know of any condition or stage of treatment where 50 mg is indicated. The risk of profound hypotension and shock is high, and the order would go to the bedside.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right now.\n- **Use a different regimen.** If the goal is stronger blood pressure control, adding a second agent is usually safer than raising amlodipine above 10 mg.\n- **Get an override.** If there's a specialist-directed protocol for this dose, pharmacy or the attending can place it through the hospital's high-dose override process. That process documents the rationale and gives a second check.\n\nIf you'd like one of the standard doses entered, tell me which."
